BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 760.19 Tm (4.4 First come first served) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 736.19 Tm (First come first served runs processes in the order they arrive. It is simple and it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 720.69 Tm (never starves a process, but a long job at the front of the queue makes every short job) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 705.19 Tm (behind it wait. This is the convoy effect.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 667.69 Tm (4.5 Shortest job first) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 643.69 Tm (Shortest job first runs the process with the smallest next CPU burst. It gives the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 628.19 Tm (smallest average waiting time when every burst is known in advance. In practice the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 612.69 Tm (next burst is only an estimate, taken from the length of the previous bursts.) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
