BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 760.19 Tm (4.7 Priority scheduling) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 736.19 Tm (Priority scheduling always runs the ready process with the highest priority. It can) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 720.69 Tm (starve a low priority process forever. Ageing fixes this by raising the priority of a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 705.19 Tm (waiting process a little on every pass, so no process waits without end.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 667.69 Tm (4.8 Summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 643.69 Tm (The scheduler chooses the next process. Preemption lets the system take the processor) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 628.19 Tm (back. Throughput, turnaround, waiting and response time pull in different directions.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 612.69 Tm (Round robin protects response time, shortest job first protects average waiting time,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.70 597.19 Tm (and priority scheduling needs ageing to stay fair.) Tj ET
endstream
